   "dress": "Linen tunics, woolen cloaks and mantles, head coverings, sandals; priests in linen robes; Roman soldiers in armor and tunic; purple garment as mock royalty.",
   "buildings_and_objects": "Stone houses with flat roofs, village wells, stone water jars, the Jerusalem temple and its courts, synagogues, rock-cut tombs closed by a rolled stone, lamps, nets and boats on the Sea of Galilee, olive groves and vineyards.",
   "technology": "Oil lamps, torches, handmade boats and nets, hand-milled grain and baked bread, wine and oil; no photography, no printed books, no firearms, no clocks; Roman roads and governor's praetorium exist."
  }
